  "compatibility": [
    "Existing plain/masked/extended/long text ABI and ordinary clients remain unchanged; the suffix and same-session scene continuity are opt-in.",
    "Only an exact OK POLL reply pairing POLICY_REQUEST with INPUT_CONTINUITY grants continuity. Old or ambiguous owners use full detach; existing clients ignore the optional bit.",
    "Ordinary continuity retains bounded passive input queues; full-focus/sleep paths retain predecessor neutralization. No application persistence before clean close/release/resume.",
    "Only X4 Home is rebuilt from its frozen selected source/flags/fonts plus the three listed overlays. Watch native Clock and selected boot remain unchanged.",
    "The optional Contexts lifetime fence preserves default object code at O1/O2/Os on both profiles and host/Xtensa; it changes no stored schema or fingerprint/rule algorithm."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "No Watch/X4 hardware execution, flash, battery, USB or display timing validation. No binaries are attached by this receipt; no SD-settings changes are made.",
    "Guarantee covers ordered edges delivered by native transports within bounded queues, not lossless physical sampling. FT6336U and GT911 providers poll physical reports and expose cached snapshots; press/release entirely between polls cannot be reconstructed. Watch buttons also use polled debounce.",
    "Scene raw FIFO is 64 edges; selected Watch native ring is 31 and X4 queue is 32. GAP/overflow neutralizes ambiguous history or fails closed while preserving custody.",
    "Virtual transport gaps and instrumented callback wall times are host-fixture measurements, not device latency. Native REDRAW denotes an attempted sleep branch, not proof of actual hardware sleep/focus transfer.",
    "Local ASan/UBSan used invocation ASAN_OPTIONS=detect_leaks=0 under ptrace. The new checkpoint CI suite uses platform-default leak detection; legacy runners retain their existing local override.",
    "X4 entry-frame checks do not prove peak call-chain stack usage."
  ],
